PalPriority adds numeric work priorities to base pals, RimWorld-style. Each pal gets a value per work type: 1 (highest) to 5 (lowest), or X (never). Pals work their most important type that currently has work available and move down their list when it runs out.

[size=4]What it does[/size]
[list]
[*]The work suitability screen (Monitoring Stand) shows a color-coded priority value in place of each checkbox — green (1) through yellow to red (5), gray X for never. Left click cycles X → 1 → … → 5 → X, right click cycles the other way.
[*]Pals you haven't configured show their default values (3 / X, from their current toggles) in a dim neutral color the moment the screen opens. Dim numbers are display-only — the pal stays fully vanilla until you click; colored numbers mean the priority engine is managing it.
[*]A pal set to Transport 1 / Mining 3 hauls until nothing needs hauling, then mines.
[*]Pending work is tracked per type (hauling, crafting, smelting, cooking, farming, mining, etc.), with a short hold so pals commit to a task instead of flip-flopping.
[*]Pals you never click are not touched by the mod at all.
[*]Priorities are stored in a config file in the mod folder. Nothing is written to save files; all in-game changes go through the game's own replicated toggle system.
[/list]

[size=4]Files[/size]
Both files are required — the mod does not function without them.
[list]
[*][b]PalPriority[/b] — the logic. Runs on whoever hosts: single player, co-op host, or dedicated server.
[*][b]PalPriorityUI[/b] — the interface. Runs on every player using the mod.
[/list]
Single player: install both.

[size=4]Installation[/size]
Requires [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/palworld/mods/3035]UE4SS (Okaetsu build)[/url].

Vortex: install both files normally; the Palworld extension places them and can install UE4SS as a dependency.

Manual: extract the [font=Courier New]ue4ss[/font] folder from each zip into [font=Courier New]Palworld\Pal\Binaries\Win64[/font], merging folders. The mods enable themselves; no mods.txt editing.

[size=4]Multiplayer[/size]
[list]
[*]The server/host runs PalPriority; every player using the mod installs PalPriorityUI.
[*]Works on dedicated servers: the server holds the priorities and syncs them to each modded player through the game's own replicated RPC channel — PalPriorityUI does not need access to the server's files. (Linux hosts need the Windows server build under Wine/Proton, standard for UE4SS.)
[*]Players without the mod installed see normal checkboxes and normal pal behavior — they are unaffected, and no mod traffic is ever sent to them.
[*]If a player removes PalPriorityUI, each of their configured pals reverts to vanilla toggles the next time they click one.
[/list]

[size=4]Notes[/size]
[list]
[*]Tested on Steam: single player, co-op host, and dedicated server.
[*]Game Pass version untested.
[*]Game updates can break UE4SS hooks. If the mod stops working after a patch, check the UE4SS console for HOOK FAILED lines and wait for an updated UE4SS build. Both scripts have a DEBUG flag at the top of main.lua that enables detailed diagnostics for bug reports.
[*]Config file: [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\PalPriority\priorities.lua[/font] — editable by hand, read at startup.
[/list]

